# 5105_ap_rmax_tie.patch is retired: it hands a tied row maximum to the HIGHEST index instead of the
# lowest, but a tie at the maximum makes the max and the second max the same value, and the
# responsibility update reads only those two values (ap_r_update), so no output can change; the
# arm passed unseen on the m2pro (2026-09-29). 5105's live arm is 5105_ap_damping.patch
x_cluster/checks/ap_noise_check.mojo	x_cluster/checks/sabotage/5122_ap_noise_round.patch
# lane hdbscan-sparse (2026-09-29): DEVIATION 1620, the sparse mutual reachability MST == the dense one (device, CPU, fit); the tie rule broken on each column
hdbscan/checks/sparse_mr_check.mojo	hdbscan/checks/sabotage/sparse_mr_device_tie.patch
hdbscan/checks/sparse_mr_check.mojo	hdbscan/checks/sabotage/sparse_mr_host_tie.patch
